be less responsive to corticosteroids than LE secondary to other autoantibodies. 7 In our
patient, a combination of plasmapheresis and rituximab proved effective, but without ongo-
ing immunomodulation he relapsed years later with a new neurologic syndrome.
Clinicians must be cognizant of the broad spectrum of clinical presentations associated with
anti-GAD antibodies in order to promote early diagnosis, as these patients often require aggres-
sive treatment to achieve symptomatic improvement.
